I need to be direct: I don't have access to previous conversations, so I can't accurately restate what I said before or recreate the specific terms I used. If I tried to reconstruct it, I'd be guessing at what you actually remember and understood, which defeats the point of checking your reasoning against what was said.

What I can do is help you think through the decision afresh, or you could re-read the previous conversation itself to verify your understanding of it. But asking me to play back something I have no record of isn't something I should attempt to do.
